   "output": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# See inside a ZIP archive\n\nsackview shows what is inside a ZIP archive before you unpack it. Use its total unpacked size to check available disk space before extracting elsewhere.\n\nInstall sackview:\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\nList the entries in an archive:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\n## Commands\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShow only entries whose names match a pattern:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\n## Good to know\n\n| Topic | Details |\n| --- | --- |\n| Archive safety | sackview never extracts entries or changes the archive. |\n| Privacy | Inspection works offline and sends no archive contents to a service. |\n| Supported formats | sackview supports ZIP archives only. Other formats produce an unsupported-format message and return exit code 24. |\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) What does sackview show you?\n(b) What command lists the entries in photos.zip?\n(c) Does sackview extract files?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (c) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
